Yes, it's possible to create a custom validation rule that blocks an issue from moving to another column if all items in a checklist are not marked as done. Here's how you can do it:

1. Go to your JIRA board and click on the "Board" menu at the top left corner of the page.
2. Select "Board settings" from the dropdown list.
3. Click on the "Validators" tab.
4. Click on the "Add validator" button.
5. Choose "ScriptRunner for JIRA" from the list of available plugins.
6. Paste the following script into the editor:

```groovy
import com.onemonkeylabs.plugin.ValidationResult

// Get the current issue
def issue = context.issue

// Get the checklist associated with the current issue
def checklist = issue.getCustomFieldValue('Checklist')

// Check if all items in the checklist are marked as done
if (checklist && checklist.items.every { item -> item.status == 'done' }) {
    // If all items are done, return an error message
    return new ValidationResult(false, "Please make sure all items in the checklist are completed before moving this issue.")
}

// If all checks pass, return true
return true
```

7. Save the script and test it by moving an issue through the affected workflow. The validation rule will prevent the issue from being moved until all items in the checklist are marked as done.

Note: This script assumes that the checklist is stored in a custom field called "Checklist". You may need to modify the script to match the name of your checklist custom field. Also, this script uses the ScriptRunner plugin, which requires a license to use. However, there are other plugins available that offer similar functionality without requiring a license. I recommend checking out the documentation for your specific JIRA version to see what plugins are available.

